Travel: third-party data, media and content
============================================

The MIT licence in LICENSE covers the source code only. Everything below keeps
its own licence. The authoritative register, with one entry per source and the
attribution line the site shows, is data/reference/licences.json.

OpenStreetMap (Open Database Licence 1.0)
  (c) OpenStreetMap contributors. https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright
  Covers the trail and route geometry in data/tracks/ (each file carries
  licence ODbL-1.0 and its attribution; see data/tracks/README.md), the place
  catalogue and lines derived from OpenStreetMap, the road routes computed by
  OpenRouteService from OpenStreetMap data, and the OpenStreetMap-derived parts
  of the globe data in web/public/globe/ and data/reference/globe/. A derived
  database published from these files is subject to the ODbL's share-alike
  terms.

GeoNames (Creative Commons Attribution 4.0)
  Contains data from GeoNames, CC BY 4.0. https://www.geonames.org/
  Covers the towns layer, data/reference/towns/ (copied verbatim from the
  GeoNames dump; source, download date and hashes in
  data/reference/towns/manifest.json).

Natural Earth (public domain)
  Made with Natural Earth. https://www.naturalearthdata.com/about/terms-of-use/
  Covers the admin-1 boundaries, regions, marine areas and rivers of the globe
  (built by tools/globe_data.py).

Wikimedia Commons (per image: Creative Commons licences or public domain)
  Photographs are hot-linked or referenced from Wikimedia Commons. The author,
  licence and source page of each image are recorded with it: the photo credits
  in web/data-snapshots/photo-credits.json, the photo fields of the records in
  data/capture/, and the trip galleries (gallery.json). Each image's own
  licence applies.

Other sources (see data/reference/licences.json for the full terms)
  world-countries (mledoze/countries), ODbL 1.0; geoBoundaries, per country
  (mostly CC BY 4.0 or ODbL); Wikidata, CC0 1.0; Government of Canada open
  data and Statistics Canada, Open Government Licence - Canada; US National
  Park Service, public domain; opendata.swiss, per dataset; Open-Meteo,
  CC BY 4.0; Copernicus Climate Change Service, Copernicus licence;
  Frankfurter and the European Central Bank reference rates.

Fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1)
  The font files in web/public/fonts/ and docs/v2/design/redesign/fonts/ are
  under the SIL Open Font License; each family's licence text is beside it
  (OFL-*.txt).

Written content (all rights reserved)
  Trip plans, notes, summaries, research prose and documentation in data/,
  research/, docs/ and legacy/ are the author's own words, written for this
  site and not licensed for reuse (data/reference/licences.json, "own-words").
  Short quotes from third-party sources in research records are attributed to
  their source.
